\b Launch guide: international.ellesmere.com\b0 \par
Ellesmere College International (ECI) \u8212? handoff for Ellesmere IT / DNS administrators\par
\b Audience:\b0  Ellesmere College IT / DNS administrators\par
\b Requested hostname:\b0  international.ellesmere.com\par
\b Purpose:\b0  Point this subdomain at the ECI web platform\par
\b Main site today:\b0  Finalsite (www.ellesmere.com \u8594? ellesmerecom.finalsite.com)\par
\b DNS provider today:\b0  GoDaddy (ns43.domaincontrol.com / ns44.domaincontrol.com)\par
\b\fs32 1. What you are being asked to do\b0\fs22\par
Ellesmere College International is launching a separate website (Next.js application with its own hosting and backend). It is not a Finalsite Composer page, microsite, or Finalsite subdomain landing page.\par
\par
Your work is almost entirely DNS. Optional Finalsite work is limited to adding a normal hyperlink from the main site navigation or an International page \u8212? not hosting the ECI app inside Finalsite.\par
\b\fs32 2. Critical: do not use the Finalsite subdomain pattern\b0\fs22\par
Finalsite\u8217?s standard docs say: create a CNAME for a subdomain \u8594? [keyword].finalsite.com, then open a Finalsite Support ticket so Composer can claim that hostname.\par
\b That pattern is wrong for this launch.\b0 \par
If international.ellesmere.com is pointed at Finalsite:\par
Finalsite will try to serve Composer content\par
The ECI platform will never receive traffic\par
SSL and auth for the ECI app will fail\par
\b Correct pattern: \b0 DNS for international points to the ECI hosting provider (CNAME target supplied by the ECI project team). Finalsite Support does not need a ticket to \u8220?claim\u8221? this hostname.\par
\b\fs32 3. Roles and hand-offs\b0\fs22\par
\par
Before DNS cutover, the ECI team must send you:\par
The CNAME target for international.ellesmere.com\par
Confirmation that the app is ready to accept that hostname\par
Preferred go-live window (optional)\par
\b\fs26 Example CNAME targets (fill in the real value from the host)\b0\fs22\par
